1
00:00:03,894 --> 00:00:07,587
Well, hello there! Today, a trick
from the "wheel walk" family:

2
00:00:07,646 --> 00:00:09,000
the "Julien walk".

3
00:00:09,066 --> 00:00:17,585
[Music]

4
00:00:17,651 --> 00:00:19,583
First things first: hand position.

5
00:00:19,649 --> 00:00:21,351
There are at least two grips.

6
00:00:21,417 --> 00:00:24,216
You can hold the saddle like this,

7
00:00:24,746 --> 00:00:28,232
which is the usual freestyle grip,
or like this.

8
00:00:28,298 --> 00:00:30,265
That's the one I use myself.

9
00:00:30,811 --> 00:00:32,351
You can hold the saddle on either side.

10
00:00:32,417 --> 00:00:34,358
It's up to you.

11
00:00:34,424 --> 00:00:37,337
Personally, I like the handle facing me,

12
00:00:37,403 --> 00:00:39,230
but the other way works just as well.

13
00:00:40,404 --> 00:00:45,471
The hand closest to my body
presses the saddle against me, here,

14
00:00:45,537 --> 00:00:47,738
as close to my groin as I can.

15
00:00:47,804 --> 00:00:51,244
Remember to bring your shoulders forward
and your head over the saddle

16
00:00:51,767 --> 00:00:53,983
for a bit of counterweight up front.

17
00:00:55,697 --> 00:00:57,924
This time, you can't practice
by holding on to a wall,

18
00:00:57,990 --> 00:01:01,765
since both hands are busy,
so you just have to go for it.

19
00:01:01,831 --> 00:01:05,737
The saddle isn't over the hub.
It sits a little further back,

20
00:01:05,803 --> 00:01:07,728
which leaves more room for your feet

21
00:01:07,794 --> 00:01:10,638
and helps balance the body,
since it's all on one side.

22
00:01:11,217 --> 00:01:14,646
At first, you can push the saddle,
put your foot against the frame,

23
00:01:14,719 --> 00:01:17,803
and just try to hold this position
for a little while.

24
00:01:20,204 --> 00:01:24,845
Once you feel safe on one foot
like this, you can go for it.

25
00:01:24,911 --> 00:01:28,884
Your weight goes on the saddle,
not too much on your feet.

26
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:32,511
It's really just like a "crab"
or a regular "wheel walk".

27
00:01:32,577 --> 00:01:35,311
Put as much of your weight
as you can on the saddle.

28
00:01:36,197 --> 00:01:38,772
You push the saddle, place your foot,

29
00:01:38,838 --> 00:01:42,464
step up, shifting your weight onto it,
and try to take a few steps.

30
00:01:43,484 --> 00:01:47,870
I push, I place, I lean on the saddle,
and I take a few steps.

31
00:01:48,984 --> 00:01:53,285
Once you can manage two or three steps,
there are two ways to go.

32
00:01:53,351 --> 00:01:56,314
Either you try
to keep it going as long as you can,

33
00:01:56,380 --> 00:01:59,424
or, and I highly recommend this,
you set yourself a goal.

34
00:01:59,490 --> 00:02:00,725
One turn, back on the pedals.

35
00:02:00,791 --> 00:02:01,890
One and a half, back on the pedals.

36
00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:03,125
Two turns, back on the pedals.

37
00:02:03,191 --> 00:02:06,190
For one turn, I set my cranks
in the direction of my little hops.

38
00:02:10,297 --> 00:02:13,363
For one and a half turns,
of course, I set them the other way.

39
00:02:13,429 --> 00:02:20,388
[Music]

40
00:02:20,454 --> 00:02:23,608
So work on both:
sometimes going as long as you can,

41
00:02:23,674 --> 00:02:28,506
sometimes setting a goal of finishing
in one turn, two, or two and a half,

42
00:02:28,572 --> 00:02:29,775
so you can see your progress.

43
00:02:29,841 --> 00:02:32,786
It's motivating, and you can use it
in a show like this,

44
00:02:32,852 --> 00:02:34,240
even if it's short.

45
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:37,741
Getting into the trick isn't very hard.

46
00:02:37,807 --> 00:02:40,267
You can do it like this,
just by starting from the cranks.

47
00:02:43,944 --> 00:02:45,258
If you know how to do a "back roll",

48
00:02:45,324 --> 00:02:47,410
it fits really nicely into combos
that start with a "back roll".

49
00:02:52,284 --> 00:02:54,771
To get back on the pedals,
leaving combos aside for now,

50
00:02:54,837 --> 00:02:56,611
you have two options.

51
00:02:56,677 --> 00:03:00,244
Either you catch the pedal
when it's at the top and ride off,

52
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:04,877
a bit like in a regular "wheel walk",
or you hop at the end

53
00:03:04,943 --> 00:03:07,191
to get your feet back on the pedals,
like at the end of a "back roll".

54
00:03:07,257 --> 00:03:09,970
I'll show you both.

55
00:03:10,036 --> 00:03:23,668
[Music]

56
00:03:23,734 --> 00:03:26,334
Once you're comfortable with this trick,
you can come up with variations.

57
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:29,661
For example, using the top of your foot
instead of the sole,

58
00:03:29,727 --> 00:03:35,655
or doing combos: there are loads
and loads of them with this trick.

59
00:03:35,721 --> 00:03:36,721
Good luck!

60
00:03:36,787 --> 00:03:59,978
[Music]

